Subject: [PATCH BlueZ v2 0/2] tools/sco-tester: Add SCO reconnect tests

Test cases for the kernel series "[PATCH v2 0/3] Bluetooth: hci_conn:
fix SCO connection reuse" (KERNEL-V2-LINK), in which a second SCO
socket connects to a device whose link is closing, in use or being
set up.

Patch 1 is v1 (https://lore.kernel.org/linux-bluetooth/20261027165059.2402360-1-yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com/)
rebased onto the mainloop-based sco-tester. Patch 2 is new: two cases
for the kernel series' patch 3, which fail with patches 1 and 2 alone.

On bluetooth-next da3cc02587c6, sco-tester has 35 cases: 31 pass
without the kernel series, 33 with its patches 1 and 2, 35 with all
three (three runs each); the failing cases are the four added here.

Please apply after the kernel series is in bluetooth-next.

Iaroslav Voitovych (2):
